StretchDD v0.02
---------------

This is a front-end to the usual tedious process of resizing a DOS
partition. To use, drop your partition into the main window, choose how much
you want to stretch it by, and press 'Stretch'.  Before doing this, make sure
you've got a copy of PRESIZER.EXE sitting on the partition so you can
re-write the partition tables from DOS afterwards.

If PRESIZER fails to extend your partition, you can use StretchDD to shrink
the partition back to its original size (i.e. you specify a negative value
to resize by).

Please note this program comes with no guarantees or warranty of any kind,
and Aleph One do not recommend resizing partitions like this if you can
possibly avoid it.  It was written for people who want to experiemnt and
don't have enough disc space to repartition 'properly'.

